-# Every other move is REFUSED with a reason, rather than silently succeeding:
-#
-#   * ``revert`` on a ``pending`` correction, or on a ``rejected`` one that was
-#     never applied, is the case the brief names: you cannot take back
-#     something that never took effect. Refused.
-#   * ``reject`` on an ``applied`` correction is refused and points at
-#     ``revert``. Both would land ``rejected``, but only one of them is true,
-#     and the caller has to say which.
-#   * ``approve`` on a ``rejected`` correction is refused. A refused correction
-#     is re-proposed by POSTing it again (which mints a fresh record with its
